# i18n Refactor Plan - locale routing & management

Status: DRAFT (awaiting decision)
Last updated: 2026-07-24

This plan evaluates whether/how to reduce the friction of the hub's i18n
implementation, and whether to rename `zh` -> `zh-Hans`. It is a planning
document - nothing is implemented yet.

---

## 1. The problem

The hub's i18n *feature* is sound (per-page fallback, never a 404 on a missing
translation, data-driven collections). The *mechanism*, however, is the
highest-friction part of the codebase:

- **Route duplication.** Every localized route has a hand-written twin under
  `src/pages/zh/`. Adding a locale means **copying the whole `zh/` tree** and
  translating UI strings. Today there are **7 route types x 2 locales = 14
  near-duplicate route files** that must be kept in sync by hand.
- **Two things to change per locale.** A contributor adding `ja` must: (1) add
  `ja` to `locales` + translate `t`/`home` (correct), AND (2) copy 7 route
  files under `src/pages/ja/` and edit locale strings (pure boilerplate).
- **Brittle sync.** The en and zh route files are near-identical; a fix in one
  must be manually mirrored in the other (this has already caused drift, e.g.
  the `basePath` prop inconsistency found during Phase 2).
- **`zh` is the legacy region form.** `zh-CN` is region-based and deprecated in
  favor of `zh-Hans` (script-based) per BCP-47 / W3C. It also blocks adding
  `zh-Hant` (Traditional) cleanly later.

The *content model* (locale dirs, slug contract, fallback) is NOT the problem
and is explicitly out of scope - it stays.

## 2. Goal

- **Adding a locale = a data change only** (`locales` + `t`/`home` strings),
  with **zero** new route files.
- Eliminate hand-synced route duplication between locales.
- Use the modern `zh-Hans` locale code.
- Keep the current URL model: default locale has **no prefix** (`/posts/foo`),
  others are prefixed (`/zh-Hans/posts/foo`).

## 3. Approaches considered

Three options were evaluated. A throwaway build experiment confirmed a key
constraint (see "Validation" below).

### Option A - Two-file pattern (default + `[locale]` for non-default)  [RECOMMENDED]

- Keep one route file per type at the top level for the **default** locale
  (`src/pages/posts/[...slug].astro` -> `/posts/foo`).
- Add **one** `src/pages/[locale]/posts/[...slug].astro` that serves **all
  non-default** locales via `getStaticPaths` looping `locales` minus the
  default (`/zh-Hans/posts/foo`, `/ja/posts/foo`, ...).
- Shared rendering logic moves into `src/lib/content.ts` (already mostly
  there); both route files become thin wrappers that pass a locale.

**File count:** 14 today -> 14 (7 default + 7 `[locale]`). Same count for 2
locales, but **adding a 3rd locale adds 0 route files** (vs +7 today). The
`[locale]` files are universal and shared across all non-default locales.

### Option B - All-prefixed + redirects (single file per type)

- Every locale (including `en`) lives under `src/pages/[locale]/...`, so there
  is **one** route file per type (7 total).
- Add `redirects` in `astro.config.mjs` so `/posts/[...slug]` -> `/en/posts/[...]`
  (Astro static `redirects` emit meta-refresh HTML + canonical).

**Trade-off:** truly fewest files, BUT it adds `/en/` to **every** URL (the
default locale is no longer prefix-free), and `/posts/foo` becomes a redirect
(canonical = `/en/posts/foo`). This changes the URL model the template has
advertised. Higher SEO/behavioral risk.

### Option C - Status quo (document better)

- Keep the mirror, improve docs/skill so the "copy the tree" step is obvious.

**Trade-off:** zero refactor risk, but does not solve the duplication or the
per-locale file cost. Drift continues.

### Validation (already performed)

A throwaway route `src/pages/[locale]/ping.astro` generating
`params: { locale: undefined }` produced **no output** - Astro silently drops
paths whose required params are `undefined`. So the tempting "single file with
an undefined locale to drop the prefix" approach **does not work** in static
output. This rules out a one-file solution that preserves the prefix-free
default, leaving Option A (two-file) or Option B (redirects) as the viable
dedup paths.

## 4. Recommendation: Option A + the `zh-Hans` rename

Option A preserves the current, good URL model (default = no prefix), makes
adding a locale a pure data change, and the `[locale]` files collapse all
non-default locales into one universal file each. It is the lowest-risk change
that actually solves the friction. Option B's URL change is not worth the file
savings for a template.

The `zh-Hans` rename is folded into the same migration so the URL/locale change
happens once.

## 5. Scope of the refactor (Option A)

### Route files

For each of the 7 route types, keep the default-locale file and replace its
`zh/` twin with a universal `[locale]/` file:

| Route | Default (keep) | New universal | Delete |
|-------|----------------|----------------|--------|
| `/` | `src/pages/index.astro` | `src/pages/[locale]/index.astro` | `zh/index.astro` |
| `/posts` | `src/pages/posts/index.astro` | `src/pages/[locale]/posts/index.astro` | `zh/posts/index.astro` |
| `/posts/[...slug]` | `src/pages/posts/[...slug].astro` | `src/pages/[locale]/posts/[...slug].astro` | `zh/posts/[...slug].astro` |
| `/posts/tags/[tag]` | `src/pages/posts/tags/[tag].astro` | `src/pages/[locale]/posts/tags/[tag].astro` | `zh/posts/tags/[tag].astro` |
| `/[product]` | `src/pages/[product]/index.astro` | `src/pages/[locale]/[product]/index.astro` | `zh/[product]/index.astro` |
| `/[product]/docs` | `src/pages/[product]/docs/index.astro` | `src/pages/[locale]/[product]/docs/index.astro` | `zh/[product]/docs/index.astro` |
| `/[product]/docs/[...slug]` | `src/pages/[product]/docs/[...slug].astro` | `src/pages/[locale]/[product]/docs/[...slug].astro` | `zh/[product]/docs/[...slug].astro` |

Locale-neutral endpoints (`404.astro`, `robots.txt.ts`) are unchanged.
`rss.xml.ts` + `zh/rss.xml.ts` collapse to one `src/pages/[locale]/rss.xml.ts`
(or stay split - minor).

### `src/lib/i18n.ts`

- `locales`: `'en'`, `'zh-Hans'`.
- `localizePath`: prefix logic is already locale-driven - no change.
- `localeFromPath`: regex `/^\/([a-z]{2}(?:-[A-Z][a-z]+)?)/` to match `zh-Hans`.
  (The current `/^\/([a-z]{2})/` would not match `zh-Hans`.)
- `buildAlternates`: already loops `locales` - no change.
- `localeLabel`: `zh-Hans: '中文'` (label unchanged; only the code).
- `localeCode`: `zh-Hans: 'zh-Hans'` (used for `toLocaleDateString`; `zh-Hans`
  is a valid BCP-47 locale for Intl in modern engines; verify in build).

### `src/lib/content.ts`

Already takes a `locale` param everywhere - the route files just need to pass
the right locale. No logic change expected; possibly a small shared helper to
render a route given a locale, to make the two wrappers trivial.

### `LocaleSwitcher.astro`

Already iterates `locales` - picks up `zh-Hans` automatically. Verify the
hreflang output (`hreflang="zh-Hans"`).

### Content dirs & docs

- `src/content/posts/zh/` -> `src/content/posts/zh-Hans/`.
- `src/content/docs/<product>/zh/` -> `.../zh-Hans/`.
- `docs/zh/` -> `docs/zh-Hans/` (the template's own synced docs), + update
  the `base: './docs'` product in `src/config/products.ts` if it references
  locale dirs (it does not - it points at the product root).
- `astro.config.mjs` sitemap `i18n.locales: { en: 'en', 'zh-Hans': 'zh-Hans' }`.

### External-repo sync skill

The `awareride-content-sync` skill and `examples/*/skills/site-content-sync`
templates use `zh/` as the locale dir name. Update the skill docs + validate
script to accept any locale in `locales` (they likely already do, since they
read the hub's `locales`), and update the example content dirs to `zh-Hans/`.

## 6. Migration steps (suggested sequencing)

1. **Branch + spike first.** Convert ONE route type end-to-end (e.g.
   `/posts/[...slug]` + its `[locale]` twin) to validate the `localeFromPath`
   regex and `toLocaleDateString` for `zh-Hans`. Confirm build + a rendered
   `/zh-Hans/posts/<slug>/` page.
2. **Rename `zh` -> `zh-Hans`** in `i18n.ts` + content dirs + docs dir + sitemap
   config. Build, fix hreflang/switcher.
3. **Convert the remaining 6 route types** to the two-file pattern, deleting the
   `zh/` twins as you go.
4. **Update sync skill + examples** for the `zh-Hans` dir name.
5. **Update docs** (`architecture.md` routing table, `authoring.md` add-a-locale
   section now becomes "add to `locales` + translate - no route files").

Each step keeps the build green and is independently committable.

## 7. Risks & mitigations

- **`toLocaleDateString('zh-Hans')` support.** Modern V8/Node 22 supports
  `zh-Hans` as a BCP-47 locale. Spike (step 1) confirms before committing.
  Fallback: keep `localeCode` mapping `zh-Hans -> 'zh-CN'` for Intl only.
- **Broken inbound links to `/zh/...`.** This is a template (no deployed SEO
  equity yet), so the rename cost is low. If preserving old URLs mattered, add
  `redirects: { '/zh/...': '/zh-Hans/...' }` - but Astro static redirects can't
  use rest-params across the whole tree, so this is impractical for a full
  rename. Accept the clean break.
- **Sync skill breakage.** External repos syncing `zh/` content would need their
  dir renamed to `zh-Hans/`. Since the examples are samples, update them; real
  consumers are few (template is new).
- **Route file count unchanged for 2 locales.** Option A keeps 14 files for 2
  locales (same as today). The win is future-locales-free + no hand-sync. Set
  this expectation in the plan; it is acceptable.

## 8. Verification

- `npm run build` -> 0 errors/warnings.
- `/posts/<slug>/` (en) and `/zh-Hans/posts/<slug>/` both render; `<html lang>`
  and `hreflang` are `zh-Hans`.
- Locale switcher offers `English` / `中文` and navigates to the `zh-Hans` URL.
- Sitemap `hreflang` entries use `zh-Hans`.
- Adding a throwaway `'ja'` to `locales` (no route files) produces a working
  `/ja/posts/<slug>/` fallback page - the proof that "adding a locale is now a
  data change."

## 9. Effort

Medium-large. Touches every route file + i18n helpers + content/doc dir
renames + sync skill. Best done as one focused PR (or 2: rename first, then
the route refactor) after a spike confirms the Intl behavior. Estimated 1
focused session.

## 10. Decision needed

- **Option A vs B vs C?** (recommend A)
- **Fold in the `zh-Hans` rename?** (recommend yes)
- **Accept the clean break on `/zh/...` URLs** (no redirects)? (recommend yes -
  template is new)
